---@class vercel.sandboxes.WriteSessionCommandStdinRequest
---@field sessionId string The unique identifier of the session containing the command.
---@field cmdId string The unique identifier of the command to write to.
---@field teamId? string The Team identifier to perform the request on behalf of.
---@field slug? string The Team slug to perform the request on behalf of.
---@field data? string Base64-encoded bytes to write to the command stdin. The request body is limited to 1 MB, so send at most about 700 KB of data per request.
---@field offset? number The position in the command stdin where `data` starts. Bytes before the total already written are skipped, so a resent request does not write them twice. Fails with 409 if it is past the bytes written so far. Without it, `data` is appended.
---@field close? boolean If true, closes the command stdin after writing `data`. Use this for commands that wait for end of input.

